# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
.venv*/

# Benchmarks: only the two small TFIM circuits are committed, as a familiarisation set. The full suite is built
# locally by benchmarks/build_suite.py, which writes the family folders, MANIFEST.csv, DROPPED.csv and build_log.txt.
# MANIFEST.example.csv holds the two committed rows; copy it to MANIFEST.csv to run the suite scripts on them.
benchmarks/*
!benchmarks/build_suite.py
!benchmarks/MANIFEST.example.csv
!benchmarks/hamsim/
benchmarks/hamsim/*
!benchmarks/hamsim/tfim_4.qasm
!benchmarks/hamsim/tfim_6.qasm

# The rule library: grown per machine by agent.py, one folder per accepted round. Not committed -- a clone starts
# with an empty playbook and builds its own. examples/givens_rule/ is the one entry that ships, as a reference.
playbook/

# Results: every table, figure and circuit under results/ is output of a campaign over one benchmark suite, so a
# clone starts empty and writes its own. The scripts that produce them are in sweep/ and baselines/.
results/

# Campaign artefacts: kept on disk, never committed.
# runs/   one folder per agent run: the workspace the agent worked in, every script it wrote,
#         transcript.jsonl, and the per-round circuits. Hundreds of MB after a full campaign.
# logs/   the chronological harness log of every stage (.md readable, .jsonl structured).
# test_out/  scratch output of tests/test_playbook.py and tests/test_ancilla_arm.py.
# .cache/claude_config  the Claude Code CLI session store; `--resume` needs it to persist between rounds.
runs/
logs/
test_out/
.cache/

# The planner study (selecting and composing stored rules): local only, not part of this repository. Its tables are
# tied to the earlier benchmark suite and its run folders are ~90 MB.
planner/

# Scratch
handoff/
